    <item>
      <title>Primetime Risks Repeating To Catch a Predator’s Mistakes</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-09-26/primetime-risks-repeating-to-catch-a-predator-s-mistakes</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">899f38dc11bbcae1188796c4</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:16 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>In a meta twist, before moviegoers experience Robert Pattinson’s portrayal of Chris Hansen in A24’s Primetime, they will see Hansen himself. The former host of the investigative series To Catch a Predator, in which Hansen confronted men seeking sex with minors, bought ads before screenings of the film. He tells the audience to “take a seat right over there” — a nod to one of his signature catchphrases — while promoting his streaming service, TruBlu, which features similar sting operations.</description>
      <dc:creator>Miles Surrey</dc:creator>
